# Line Trimming and Whitespace Rules

## Required Formatting

* **Remove all trailing whitespace** from the end of every line
* **No trailing spaces** after any line of code, comments, or text
* **No extra blank lines** at the end of files
* **Consistent indentation** - use spaces or tabs consistently within each file
* **Single empty line** between logical sections when appropriate
* **No multiple consecutive empty lines** - maximum one empty line between sections

## Examples

**✅ Correct (no trailing spaces):**

```typescript
function process(data: string) {
  const result = data.trim();
  return result;
}
```

**❌ Incorrect (has trailing spaces):**

```typescript
function process(data: string) {   
  const result = data.trim();   
  return result;   
}   
```

## Implementation

* **Always trim** trailing whitespace when editing any file
* **Clean up** existing trailing spaces when touching a file
* **Validate** that lines end cleanly without extra spaces
* **Maintain** consistent formatting throughout the codebase

## File Types

This rule applies to all text-based files including:

* Source code files (`.ts`, `.js`, `.tsx`, `.jsx`, etc.)
* Configuration files (`.json`, `.yaml`, `.md`, etc.)
* Documentation files (`.md`, `.txt`, etc.)
* Test files and any other text content
